name: test and logic
boss: TestCase
flavor: Every question I ask has exactly two answers.
brief: [ is a command, not syntax. That is why it needs spaces around it and a
brief: closing ] as its last argument -- it is reading arguments like anything
brief: else. test is the same command without the bracket.
brief:
brief: It answers by exit status, so it slots straight into if, && and ||.
brief:
brief: Quote your variables. [ -n $x ] with x empty becomes [ -n ], which is
brief: true, which is the opposite of what you asked. [ -n "$x" ] is correct.
